{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.NormalizedSumTelescopeBridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.NormalizedSumTelescopeBridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.NormalizedSumTelescopeBridge.one_sub_qsq_pow_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.NormalizedSumTelescopeBridge.one_sub_qsq_pow_eq","kind":"theorem","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/NormalizedSumTelescopeBridge.lean#L31-L44","doc":"**Per-cell denominator bridge.** The Macdonald per-cell denominator factor `1 − q^{2h}` (the\n`1 − Q^{h}` of `schurElement` at `Q = q²`) equals `−q^{h}·(q − q⁻¹)·[h]_q` in terms of the balanced\nhook bracket. Chained over the cells of `λ`, this converts `∏_x 1/(1 − q^{2 h_x})` into\n`(−1)^{|λ|} q^{−Σh} (q − q⁻¹)^{−|λ|} / hookProd_q(λ)`, the numerator side of the convention bridge. ","signatureChunk":0}]}